    <briefdescription>
<para>Extracts statutory and case-law citations from legal documents. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Matches German-law citation patterns:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Statutory references: &quot;§ 242 BGB&quot;, &quot;Art. 14 Abs. 1 GG&quot;</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Court decisions: &quot;BGH, Urt. v. 14.12.2021, II ZR 93/21&quot; &quot;BVerwG, Beschl. v. 3.5.2022 – 4 B 12/22&quot;</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>EU/ECHR citations: &quot;EuGH, C-123/21&quot;, &quot;EGMR 12345/20&quot;</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para>Each matched citation becomes a CITATION-modality <ref refid="structthemis_1_1training_1_1_training_sample" kindref="compound">TrainingSample</ref> whose <computeroutput>input</computeroutput> is the citation text and <computeroutput>output</computeroutput> is the inferred citation type (e.g., &quot;statutory&quot;, &quot;case_law&quot;, &quot;eu_regulation&quot;). </para>
    </detaileddescription>
